Subject: [PATCH] feat(openorcreate,test): add data-action anchors for open-or-create dialog (G6.2)

Staged for Phase G6.2 "new project" end-to-end journey test. The
DialogOpenOrCreateProject component in
`packages/app/src/components/dialog-open-or-create-project.tsx` has no
stable `data-action` anchors — the create/choose/name/submit affordances
are reachable only via visible (i18n-dependent) text or via Kobalte
component tags, both of which are brittle for an end-to-end flow test.

This patch adds:
- data-action="openorcreate-create" on the "Create New Folder" tile
  (the button in the choice screen that switches mode to create)
- data-action="openorcreate-existing" on the "Open Existing Folder" tile
  (the button in the choice screen that triggers onOpenExisting)
- data-action="openorcreate-name-input" on the TextField for the new
  project name (so tests can target the <input> host reliably)
- data-action="openorcreate-parent-button" on the parent-picker trigger
  (the ghost Button that invokes openDirectoryPickerDialog). The native
  picker itself is out-of-reach from MCP; tests that need to bypass it
  either drive creation via the project_fs Tauri command directly (see
  tests/ipc/test_project_fs.py) or, once this lands, stub
  platform.openDirectoryPickerDialog in test mode.
- data-action="openorcreate-submit" on the primary "Create and open"
  button (so the submit path has a stable anchor independent of the
  busy/localized button text).

Pairs with tests/flows/test_journey_new_project.py (xfail-staged until
this patch lands on gpd-app main).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/packages/app/src/components/dialog-open-or-create-project.tsx b/packages/app/src/components/dialog-open-or-create-project.tsx
--- a/packages/app/src/components/dialog-open-or-create-project.tsx
+++ b/packages/app/src/components/dialog-open-or-create-project.tsx
@@ -80,6 +80,7 @@ export const DialogOpenOrCreateProject: Component<DialogOpenOrCreateProjectProps
             <button
               type="button"
               class="flex items-center gap-4 rounded-lg border border-border-weaker-base hover:border-border-weak-base bg-surface-raised-base hover:bg-surface-raised-stronger-base transition-colors px-4 py-3 text-left"
+              data-action="openorcreate-existing"
               onClick={() => {
                 dialog.close()
                 props.onOpenExisting()
@@ -95,6 +96,7 @@ export const DialogOpenOrCreateProject: Component<DialogOpenOrCreateProjectProps
             <button
               type="button"
               class="flex items-center gap-4 rounded-lg border border-border-weaker-base hover:border-border-weak-base bg-surface-raised-base hover:bg-surface-raised-stronger-base transition-colors px-4 py-3 text-left"
+              data-action="openorcreate-create"
               onClick={() => setMode("create")}
             >
               <Icon name="plus" size="large" class="text-text-weak shrink-0" />
@@ -116,6 +118,7 @@ export const DialogOpenOrCreateProject: Component<DialogOpenOrCreateProjectProps
           <TextField
             label={language.t("home.combinedPicker.create.nameLabel")}
             placeholder={language.t("home.combinedPicker.create.namePlaceholder")}
+            data-action="openorcreate-name-input"
             value={name()}
             onChange={(v) => setName(v)}
             autofocus
@@ -125,7 +128,7 @@ export const DialogOpenOrCreateProject: Component<DialogOpenOrCreateProjectProps
               {language.t("home.combinedPicker.create.parentLabel")}
             </div>
             <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
-              <Button variant="ghost" size="normal" onClick={pickParent}>
+              <Button variant="ghost" size="normal" onClick={pickParent} data-action="openorcreate-parent-button">
                 <Icon name="folder-add-left" size="small" />
                 {language.t("home.combinedPicker.create.chooseParent")}
               </Button>
@@ -147,6 +150,7 @@ export const DialogOpenOrCreateProject: Component<DialogOpenOrCreateProjectProps
             <Button
               size="normal"
               disabled={busy() || !name().trim() || !parent()}
+              data-action="openorcreate-submit"
               onClick={submitCreate}
             >
               {busy() ? language.t("home.combinedPicker.create.creating") : language.t("home.combinedPicker.create.submit")}

Note: even with these anchors, driving the full dialog flow requires
stubbing `platform.openDirectoryPickerDialog` (the native picker cannot
be automated via MCP). The harness test uses a small setter on
`window.__OPENCODE__.platform.openDirectoryPickerDialog` (or similar
test-only override) to return a tmp parent path deterministically. If
that test hook also requires a product-side change, a follow-up
`G6-platform-picker-test-hook.patch` will be staged separately.
